Every year tens of people around the world are killed by birds.

264
00:13:45,670 --> 00:13:48,200
I'm not going to be another statistic.

265
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:52,120
Look how sweet he is. Come over and say hi.

266
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,450
Come on.

267
00:13:57,450 --> 00:13:58,880
You can do it.

268
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,560
Don't be scared.

269
00:14:00,930 --> 00:14:01,350
Come on.

270
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:06,620
Oh, just pet the bird, you big baby!

271
00:14:13,870 --> 00:14:15,600
I did it!

272
00:14:17,370 --> 00:14:19,540
I actually did it.

273
00:14:19,870 --> 00:14:21,360
Okay, now flush him.

274
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:27,550
So, Leonard, what do you do for fun?

275
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:29,240
I'm... let's see.

276
00:14:29,670 --> 00:14:31,100
Hiking.

277
00:14:32,610 --> 00:14:35,390
Karaoke in Koreatown.

278
00:14:35,990 --> 00:14:38,050
Any Jennifer Aniston movie.

279
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:40,900
Hey. Sorry I ditched you.

280
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,950
- No, it's fine. You can ditch away.  - Oh, no, no.

281
00:14:42,950 --> 00:14:44,300
We said we were going to hang out, let's hang out.

282
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:46,030
It's cool. Go back to Kevin.

283
00:14:46,030 --> 00:14:47,700
Oh, he had to leave.

284
00:14:48,010 --> 00:14:49,460
Interesting.

285
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:51,830
So now that he's gone, you want to hang out with me.

286
00:14:51,830 --> 00:14:53,430
- This must be Penny.  - Yep.

287
00:14:53,430 --> 00:14:55,960
I totally get it.

288
00:14:58,670 --> 00:15:00,640
Huh? I'm sorry, get what?

289
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:02,520
Don't worry about it. You know, there's some guys over there.

290
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:03,310
You should go talk to them.

291
00:15:03,310 --> 00:15:05,130
No, no. I want to know what you told her.

292
00:15:05,130 --> 00:15:07,330
That's kind of between me and...

293
00:15:07,330 --> 00:15:09,260
- Laura.  - Laura.

294
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:10,900
Oh. Okay, I see.

295
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:13,990
So while he was telling you things,did he mention he owns,

296
00:15:13,990 --> 00:15:16,390
not one, but two Star Trek uniforms?

297
00:15:16,390 --> 00:15:18,490
- Really?  - Yeah. Wears them.

298
00:15:18,490 --> 00:15:20,960
Not just for Halloween.

299
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,200
Hey, pal.

300
00:15:25,670 --> 00:15:27,630
You didn't see me telling Kevin that

301
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:31,100
you thought cold wars were only fought in winter.

302
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:35,340
Okay. Then I'll return the favor, and I won't tell...

303
00:15:35,340 --> 00:15:36,740
- Laura. ...  - Laura

304
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:40,880
that half the dirty movies you own are animated.

305
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:48,220
When you were telling Kevin about your acting career,

306
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:51,180
did you mention your long-running role as "Waitress"

307
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:54,510
in a local production of The Cheese Factory?

308
00:15:55,570 --> 00:15:58,410
Did you tell her about your lucky asthma inhaler?

309
00:15:59,110 --> 00:16:01,500
Oh, yeah? Spell "asthma."

310
00:16:03,410 --> 00:16:05,710
A-s...

311
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,230
Take me home.

312
00:16:08,430 --> 00:16:10,030
Maybe I'm not done hanging out with...

313
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:14,360
You're right, it's getting late.

314
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:22,870
It's remarkable.

315
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:25,240
All that time spent in fear.

316
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:27,140
And for what?

317
00:16:27,150 --> 00:16:28,850
He's magnificent.

318
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,210
Oh, dear.

319
00:16:31,210 --> 00:16:34,600
I just realized I haven't offered you a beverage.

320
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:44,390
Oh, it's just like my grandma with her parrot.

321
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:48,900
And after she lost her marbles with her remote control.

322
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:52,970
My phone's on the desk over there.

323
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:55,050
Take a picture of us together.

324
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:59,210
Make it good enough to go on a mug, a mouse pad, and a calendar.

325
00:17:04,550 --> 00:17:07,420
If you were a dove, I'd call you Lovey-Dovey.

326
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:09,110
Oh. Who am I kidding?

327
00:17:09,110 --> 00:17:11,350
This isn't a moment for strict adherence to the literal.

328
00:17:11,350 --> 00:17:14,220
You're just my little Lovey-Dovey, aren't you?

329
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:17,450
Guess you gotta have hollow bones

330
00:17:17,450 --> 00:17:19,090
to get some sugar around here.

331
00:17:21,970 --> 00:17:24,530
I still think he looks like someone's pet.

332
00:17:24,530 --> 00:17:26,600
Maybe we should put up posters.

333
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,970
Yes. It should have a big picture of him,

334
00:17:28,970 --> 00:17:33,300
and the words, "Is this your bird? Not anymore."

335
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:37,370
We're going to have so much fun together.

336
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:40,330
You can carry messages to all my enemies.

337
00:17:41,450 --> 00:17:45,030
I can tie a string to your leg and fly you like a kite.

338
00:17:45,870 --> 00:17:48,110
If you're keeping him, I've got a cage you can borrow.

339
00:17:48,110 --> 00:17:50,000
One of the test monkeys slipped on a banana peel

340
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,480
and broke his neck.

341
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:56,150
It was both tragic and hysterical.

342
00:17:58,420 --> 00:17:59,780
Nonsense.

343
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:02,920
No. Lovey-Dovey doesn't sleep in a cage.

344
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:06,260
No. Lovey-Dovey sleeps in his very own nest,

345
00:18:06,260 --> 00:18:09,730
which I'm going to get off the windowsill and put in my room.

346
00:18:09,730 --> 00:18:12,100
Isn't that right, LD?

347
00:18:16,370 --> 00:18:17,640
No.

348
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,270
Where are you going?

349
00:18:19,270 --> 00:18:21,370
Come back, Lovey-Dovey!

350
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:23,040
This is your home now!

351
00:18:23,050 --> 00:18:27,250
I already ordered 20 pounds of bird feed off of Amazon!

352
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:30,020
He's gone.

353
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:32,290
I'm sorry, Sheldon.

354
00:18:32,610 --> 00:18:34,740
How could he do this to me?

355
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:38,950
Get back here, you stupid bird, so I can love you!

356
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:17,920
Okay. So... we went out,

357
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:20,490
saw a movie, met some nice people,

358
00:19:20,490 --> 00:19:22,820
said horrible things about each other in public...

359
00:19:22,820 --> 00:19:25,160
all in all, a pretty magical night.

360
00:19:25,890 --> 00:19:27,330
Okay, I'm not innocent in all this,

361
00:19:27,330 --> 00:19:31,330
but you basically called me stupid, you asthmatic dumbass.

362
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:35,440
I know, I-I-I crossed a line.

363
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:37,170
And I'm sorry.

364
00:19:37,170 --> 00:19:39,400
No, no, no, hang on. I really mean it.

365
00:19:39,410 --> 00:19:41,130
And it's not like when we were going out,

366
00:19:41,130 --> 00:19:43,960
I'd just apologize for everything so we could end up in bed.

367
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:49,800
This is a 100% sex-is-off-the-table "I'm sorry."

368
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:52,040
All right. Thank you.

369
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,270
I'm sorry, too.

370
00:19:53,910 --> 00:19:56,500
Just to be clear, sex is off the table, right?

371
00:19:57,890 --> 00:19:59,150
Way off.

372
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:03,960
Maybe we're not ready to hang out as friends.

373
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:06,350
I don't know. Up until the last part,

374
00:20:06,350 --> 00:20:08,440
I was kind of enjoying take-charge Leonard

375
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:10,120
with a little backbone.

376
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:11,970
Picking the movie, knowing what he wants,

377
00:20:11,970 --> 00:20:13,510
a little cocky.

378
00:20:13,910 --> 00:20:15,610
- Really?  - Yeah.

379
00:20:16,020 --> 00:20:19,230
Well, then, I'm putting sex back on the table.

380
00:20:22,690 --> 00:20:24,220
What do you think about that?

381
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:27,320
- Ooh. Maybe I like it. - You do?

382
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,230
Because if that's what you like, I can be that guy.

383
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:30,990
I swear, I'll be anything you want me to be.

384
00:20:31,790 --> 00:20:33,660
Good night, Leonard.

385
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:41,240
I am such an asthmatic dumbass.

386
00:20:42,870 --> 00:20:44,640
I had a weird night.

387
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:47,080
Mine was great.

388
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:49,810
I'm going to be a mommy!

